### A residual made only of sixth and seventh derivatives.
###
###   R = u_6x - u_7x + u_6y - u_7y = 0   on [-1,1]^2
###   u* = exp(x) + exp(y)
###
### f^(6) - f^(7) = 0 is satisfied exactly by f = exp, so the solution is
### known.  The point of the case is that the residual contains no low
### order term at all: in bench/zk7 the residual mixes orders one through
### seven, and a network can satisfy it while each order is individually
### wrong because the errors cancel.  Here there is nothing to cancel
### against, so the sixth and seventh derivatives have to be right on
### their own.
###
### The operator has a large null space, and the boundary data does NOT
### remove it.  With L = D^6 - D^7, G(s) = 1 - s^2 and
###
###   F(s) = s^8 + 8 s^7 + 28 s^6 - 8 s - 29 ,
###
### one has F(+-1) = G(+-1) = 0, L G = 0 and L F = -20160 G, so
###
###   h(x,y) = F(x) G(y) - G(x) F(y)
###
### vanishes on the whole boundary and satisfies (L_x + L_y) h = 0, while
### its own sixth and seventh derivatives are not zero (d^6h/dx^6 is
### about 2.9e4 at (0.3, 0.4)).  Hence exp(x) + exp(y) + c h(x,y) solves
### the same problem with the same boundary values for every c, and it
### changes the individual high derivatives.
###
### So this case does NOT show that the sixth and seventh derivatives are
### individually right: their errors can cancel between the two terms of
### the residual even though no lower-order term is present.  What it does
### exercise is the combined residual and the weight gradient of it, at an
### order where nothing else in the suite reaches.  The reported solution
### error is against one member of the family, the one training selects.
Init_w       Glorot_norm
Rand_seed    20260802 /
Restart      0 /
Output_deriv 0 /

Nlayer       4 / L
2 / ndim(1) = D0 = (x, y)
24 /
24 /
1 / ndim(L)

Loss_term  DATA         160  data.dat    1.d0  / the boundary
Loss_term  COLLOCATION  400  colloc.dat  1.d-2 / the interior

Residual 4 /
LIN   1.d0    6 0 /   u_6x
LIN  -1.d0    7 0 /  -u_7x
LIN   1.d0    0 6 /   u_6y
LIN  -1.d0    0 7 /  -u_7y
Exact_solution 1 /

Hod_K      7 /
1.d0
0.d0
0.d0
0.d0
0.d0
0.d0
0.d0
0.d0
Hod_dense  0 /   the closure of the residual indices

Hod_check  1 /
Num_validation 40 /
Validation_cyc 500 /
P_max          2000 /
Epoch      20000 /
Activation TANH /
Conv       1.d-14 /
Num_batch  40 /
Checkpoint_cyc 100000 /
GD_method  Adam
GD_param   0.002d0 0.9d0 0.999d0 1.d-8 0.d0 /
